  "question": {
    "text": "The number of integral values of <math><mi>c</mi></math> for which both the roots of the equation <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> are greater than <math><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> but less than <math><mn>4</mn></math> are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "more than <math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></math><br />Hence, the number of integral values of <math><mi>c</mi></math> are <math><mn>3</mn></math>."
  }
